  *   1  read-only: the G3D power domains' state; GPU_ID and friends only if
  *      the top domain is already on.
  *   2  also power the top domain on (if off) and then read the registers.
+ *   3  also boot the CSF firmware on the MCU and ping it (see below).
  *
  * Facts (zuma-gpu.dtsi, zuma-pm-domains.dtsi, cal-if zuma
  * flexpmu_cal_local_zuma.h, exynos-pd_el3.c, Arm Mali CSF register map as in
@@ -24,6 +25,31 @@
  *   0x18, CSF_ID 0x1C, SHADER_PRESENT 0x100/0x104, TILER_PRESENT 0x110,
  *   L2_PRESENT 0x120, GPU_STATUS 0x34.
  *
+ * MCU firmware boot (huskygpu=3), following Linux panthor (panthor_fw.c,
+ * panthor_gpu.c, panthor_mmu.c) and Google's zuma kbase r54p3 for the Pixel
+ * specifics:
+ * - firmware: mali_csffw-r54p3.bin from the phone's /vendor/firmware, handed
+ *   over by the boot payload as /chosen/memory-map HuskyGPUFW. Header: magic
+ *   0xC3F13A6E, version minor/major at +4/+5, entry-stream size at +0x10,
+ *   entries from +0x14: u32 header (type 7:0, size 15:8, OPTIONAL bit 31);
+ *   type 0 = IFACE section: flags, va start/end, data start/end. Flags: RD 0,
+ *   WR 1, EX 2, cache mode 4:3 (1 = cached), PROT 5 (skipped: protected
+ *   memory), SHARED 30, ZERO 31. The SHARED section at VA 0x04000000 is the
+ *   global interface.
+ * - order: IRQ masks 0; soft reset (GPU_COMMAND 0x0101, GPU_IRQ_RAWSTAT bit
+ *   8); COHERENCY_ENABLE 0x304 = 31 (none; zuma's GPU is not coherent); L2
+ *   slice hash ASN_HASH 0x2C0.. = DT l2-hash-values, L2_CONFIG 0x48 bit 24;
+ *   L2_PWRON 0x1A0 / L2_READY 0x160; MCU page tables (4 KiB granule, 4 levels,
+ *   48-bit VA) in AS0: TRANSTAB 0x2400, MEMATTR 0x2408 = 0x4C4C4C4C8C4C8F4C
+ *   (index 0 non-cacheable, 1 write-back), TRANSCFG 0x2430 = 0x420001C6,
+ *   AS_COMMAND 0x2418 = UPDATE, AS_STATUS 0x2428; JOB_IRQ clear, MCU_CONTROL
+ *   0x700 = AUTO (2); boot = JOB_IRQ_RAWSTAT 0x1000 bit 31 and GLB_VERSION != 0.
+ * - global interface (shared+0): version, features, input VA, output VA;
+ *   requests toggle GLB_REQ bits against GLB_ACK, then doorbell 0 (0x80000).
+ * Firmware and page-table pages are written through the cacheable mapping and
+ * cleaned to DRAM (non-coherent walks); the shared section is accessed only
+ * through a non-cacheable alias.
+ *
  * Every step is logged (kprintf too) before it runs, so an SError leaves a
  * trail in pmsg.
  */
